# Python virtualenvs / caches. `**/` matters: DTLibrary/.venv is a full CUDA
# torch install (~5.7 GB) sitting under the COPY source of the root Dockerfile,
# and a bare `.venv` pattern only matches the repo-root one.
.venv
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info

# Node. The frontend is built from ./frontend, never from this context.
**/node_modules
frontend/dist

# VCS / CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Secrets — compose passes these in as environment variables instead.
.env

# Docs and data no image reads. Keeping these out shrinks the context transfer;
# `demo/` alone is 151 MB.
*.md
docs/
readme_en/
tests/
benchmarks/
conversation_logs/
conversation_logs.zip
demo/
images/
logs/
pychrono_results/
